-- #1216 ARM 2 — THE DRAIN CELL, and the NAMED-FIELD-VARIANT sibling of
-- `record_xmod_field_order/` (which is the same defect in its short-form-record
-- spelling, drained by #1382).
--
-- Two modules each declare a constructor `Cfg` with the same two `Int` field names at
-- OPPOSITE indices, under DIFFERENT owning types (`WrapA` / `WrapZ`).  They do not
-- import each other and neither projects the other's record: every `.a`/`.b` happens
-- inside the module that declared it.
--
-- 🚨 THE ENTRY NEVER MENTIONS `Cfg`, `WrapA` OR `WrapZ`.  It imports four plain `Int`
-- values.  A module's OWN projections were being corrupted by a declaration it has no
-- import path to — the `AGENTS.md` "unrelated code breaks" shape.
--
-- WHY IT IS A DIFFERENT ARM FROM `record_xmod_field_order/`, not a restatement: there
-- the head tycon IS the registry key (`Cfg`), so `lookupRecordByMangledHead`'s
-- suffix filter finds `<mid>__Cfg` candidates and #1382's narrowing resolves it.  Here
-- the head is `WrapA`/`WrapZ` while the key is `Cfg`, so NO key suffix-matches
-- `__WrapA`, the candidate list is EMPTY, that narrowing never runs, and control fell
-- to `resolveFieldByOwners` → `pairRecordByName (headL owners)` — the first key in
-- `sortUniqS` order, i.e. by MODULE-NAME SORT ORDER.
--
-- ⚠️ EVAL IS A KNOWN-WRONG ORACLE HERE, IN THE REASSURING DIRECTION, so this golden was
-- NOT taken from `medaka run`.  The interpreter resolves fields by NAME at run time
-- (`evalField (VRecord _ fields) field = fieldOr fields field`, `compiler/eval/eval.mdk`),
-- so it printed the correct answer throughout the whole life of the bug.  What this
-- cell grades is the EXECUTED NATIVE (and WasmGC) BINARY.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND from the sources before anything was run:
--   awrap: mkA = Cfg { a = 11, b = 22 }  =>  arA = 11, arB = 22
--   zwrap: mkZ = Cfg { b = 33, a = 44 }  =>  zrA = 44, zrB = 33
-- so `11,22,44,33`.
--
-- Counterfactual, MEASURED rather than reasoned: on a binary cold-built from the merge
-- base, `medaka check` exits 0, `medaka run` prints `11,22,44,33`, `medaka build` exits
-- 0, and the EXECUTED BINARY prints `11,22,33,44` — zwrap's own two fields silently
-- swapped, at exit 0, with no diagnostic anywhere.
import awrap.{arA, arB}
import zwrap.{zrA, zrB}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  putStrLn
    (intToString arA ++ "," ++ intToString arB ++ "," ++ intToString zrA ++ "," ++ intToString zrB)
